What is it?
~~~~~~~~~~~
    This program will display to a user their own unique up/download status
and account information. The following information is displayed:

    Handle & Account Number.
    Their Total UpLoaded   Files & Bytes.
    Their Total DownLoaded Files & Bytes.
    The Total Number of Uploaded   Files & Bytes in the SYSTEM.
    The Total Number of Downloaded Files & Bytes in the SYSTEM.
    The User's File & Byte Ratio.
    The User's File & Byte Credits.
    The User's Pfile Game Points.

    --- and (this one's neat) ---

    The LAST TWO Downloaded Files WITH Byte Sizes MADE BY THE USER!
    The LAST TWO Uploaded   Files WITH Byte Sizes MADE BY THE USER!

How do I set it up?
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    With this Archive should be the following files:

        UserUDStats         - The Command File That Displays The Screen.
        UserUDStats.LastDL  - The Routine That Reads LAST TWO DOWNLOADS.
        UserUDStats.LastUL  - The Routine That Reads LAST TWO UPLOADS.

    After the mod is installed, and after the first UL or DL has occurred,
a fourth file will be created:

        UserUDStats.Data    - This file contains the LAST U/D Data.

    The ".Data" file is self starting and self sufficient. It will house the
information needed to display the LAST Downloads and Uploads for ALL YOUR
users. It does this by reading the "uloads" and "dloads" logs, so you will
need to be using these two logs. Your CNet comes with these logs already
created. All you have to be concerned with here is that you didn't change
the NAMES of the logs. They must be "uloads" and "dloads" respectively in
order for this mod to work.

    You should place ALL Files starting with "UserUDStats" in your PFILES:
directory. The ".Data" file will also be created there. You must also make
the following two changes to your BBSTEXT file, so that the support files
will be executed at the completion of every upload or download:

    Load your BBSTEXT into a text editor, then go to line 466. It should be
this line:

        \n1Please enter a short description for this file.\n1:

    You need to ADD the following in FRONT of everything else on that line,
so the completed line should look like this:

\#0pfiles:UserUDStats.LastUL\\n1Please enter a short description... etc.
^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^|^^
This is what you should ADD!!

    After you finish with that line, go to line 575, which should be:

        \q0\n1Transfer successful!\n1

    You need to ADD the following in FRONT of this line as well. The line
should look like this when your done:

        \#0pfiles:UserUDStats.LastDL\\q0\n1Transfer successful!\n1
        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^|^^
        This is what you should ADD!!

    Be sure not to press ENTER or acidentally DELETE any lines from BBSTEXT
or you'll be asking Mr. Guru to stop by your place. Simply INSERT the above
information into the 2 given lines and RESAVE your BBSTEXT file.

    The only thing left to do is insert the file somewhere your users will
be able to see it, like a logon menu, or from the Pfiles, or even as the
UD Entry Screen. Wherever you decide to insert it, the command will be the
same:

        \#0pfiles:UserUDStats\

    The screen has been created to fit nicely on a 23 row screen, but if you
plan to place it somewhere that will have the screen CLEAR right after the
screen is shown, you may wish to place a line that waits for the ENTER key
to be pressed. Here's how you can add a line that does just that into a CNet
text file like "sys.welcome":

    \cfPress \c6ENTER \cfnow...\i1

